Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
------------------------------------------------  
STORMS_20XX (each yearly table in NOAA_DATA_PLUS.NOAA_HISTORIC_SEVERE_STORMS)  
• "event_type": filter to hail events (`ILIKE '%hail%'`).  
• "event_point": point in WKB; convert with `ST_GEOGFROMWKB()` and use for spatial join.  
• "event_latitude", "event_longitude": fallback for building a point with `ST_POINT()`.  
• "event_begin_time": (micro‑seconds since epoch) could be used for extra date checks, but selecting only 2014‑2024 tables already limits the period.  
• "state_fips_code", "state": optional extra filters / results.  

GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES  
• "zip_code_geom": polygon in WKB; convert with `ST_GEOGFROMWKB()`; used with `ST_WITHIN()` to see if a storm point falls inside the ZIP polygon.  
• "zip_code": final answer (top ZIPs).  
• "city", "state_code", "state_name": optional context.  

Typical conditions that may be used  
• "event_type" ILIKE '%hail%'  
• Tables restricted to years 2014 – 2024 (`STORMS_2014 … STORMS_2024`).  
• `ST_WITHIN( ST_GEOGFROMWKB(s."event_point"), ST_GEOGFROMWKB(z."zip_code_geom") )` = TRUE  

10 exploratory–to–final SQL queries  
------------------------------------  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at distinct event types recorded in 2020 to confirm the exact spelling for hail.
SELECT DISTINCT "event_type"
FROM "NOAA_DATA_PLUS"."NOAA_HISTORIC_SEVERE_STORMS"."STORMS_2020"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show a few records that look like hail in 2020.
SELECT *
FROM "NOAA_DATA_PLUS"."NOAA_HISTORIC_SEVERE_STORMS"."STORMS_2020"
WHERE "event_type" ILIKE '%hail%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Inspect the raw WKB in the event_point field for hail rows (2020).
SELECT "event_id", "event_point"
FROM "NOAA_DATA_PLUS"."NOAA_HISTORIC_SEVERE_STORMS"."STORMS_2020"
WHERE "event_type" ILIKE '%hail%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Preview a handful of ZIP polygons to ensure geometry is present.
SELECT "zip_code", "zip_code_geom"
FROM "NOAA_DATA_PLUS"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Build a hail point from lat/long (if event_point appears NULL) to verify geography creation.
SELECT "event_id",
       ST_POINT("event_longitude", "event_latitude") AS "evt_geog"
FROM "NOAA_DATA_PLUS"."NOAA_HISTORIC_SEVERE_STORMS"."STORMS_2020"
WHERE "event_type" ILIKE '%hail%' 
  AND "event_latitude" IS NOT NULL
  AND "event_longitude" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Test a spatial join between hail events (2020) and ZIP polygons.
SELECT s."event_id",
       z."zip_code"
FROM "NOAA_DATA_PLUS"."NOAA_HISTORIC_SEVERE_STORMS"."STORMS_2020"  s
JOIN "NOAA_DATA_PLUS"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"              z
  ON ST_WITHIN(
        ST_GEOGFROMWKB(s."event_point"),
        ST_GEOGFROMWKB(z."zip_code_geom")
     )
WHERE s."event_type" ILIKE '%hail%'
LIMIT 20;
